  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (recorded as cash). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); business-type from the proprietary funds statement Total column (p7), whose roll-forward is net position (cash and certificates of deposit, no liabilities). Business-type statement prints separate operating and nonoperating sections; receipts total = 203,018 + 10,736 computed; disbursements total 365,906 = Statement of Activities business-type expenses (p2) = operating 256,478 + nonoperating 109,428. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (totals equal the government-wide governmental column, p1) plus proprietary lines from p6; totals from the Statement of Net Position Total column (p1). Detail: General Fund from the departmental combining statement (pp11-12; it supersedes the General Fund budgetary comparison on p9, not recorded to avoid double counting); Street Fund from its budget schedule (p10; budget-only Loan proceeds and Transfers lines with zero actual omitted). Water and Sewer have no schedule, so no detail lines. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
